{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1129130-changing-the-tribe","id":1129130,"title":"Changing the tribe","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-14T23:47:47-07:00","id":1129130,"title":"Changing the tribe","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> a couple of year now, I have an idea for a character or character development over a campaign: Get of Fenris, Warrior (the Archetype ;-)) sick of war as the only solution becoming a Stargazer. My question is: Is this possible? Is it possible to change your tribe, go into another one?<br /> thanks a lot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14333-judgefredd","name":"JudgeFredd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T04:57:57-07:00","id":1129184,"title":"","content":"Yes, but you lose all rank and potentially lose some of your gifts depending on the storyteller. There is a rite for renouncing your Tribe and then you go through the initiation rite for the new tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T05:52:29-07:00","id":1129193,"title":"","content":"There is potentially also some pushback for leaving the Fenrir. Depending on the setting, the Stargazers might have actually left the Nation as well, which would cause further issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T08:59:49-07:00","id":1129253,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks.<br /> You can loose a gift? Are the gifts linked to the tribal totem?<br /> Didn't the stargazers leave in W20? I thought that was a nice story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14333-judgefredd","name":"JudgeFredd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T09:03:55-07:00","id":1129254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JudgeFredd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1129130-changing-the-tribe?p=1129253#post1129253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, thanks.<br /> You can loose a gift? Are the gifts linked to the tribal totem?<br /> Didn't the stargazers leave in W20? I thought that was a nice story.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd probably just lose any Tribal Gifts. Breed and Auspice Gifts would remain because you're not changing your Breed or Auspice, just your Tribe.<br /> <br /> As for the Stargazers, they left in the Metaplot of the Rev Ed and joined up with the Beast Courts. At least most of them, some lingered in the Garou Nation. W20 leaves their status in the Garou Nation up to the Storyteller and Players, as with much of the metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:48:05-07:00","id":1129331,"title":"","content":"You shouldn't be losing Gifts. They're changes made to the Garou's spirit half that aren't readily undone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T15:10:11-07:00","id":1129447,"title":"","content":"No you don't lose Tribal Gifts, its just that gifts Related to Fenrir Totems and spirits, especially those who ask for their favor will demand greater chiminage in order to test your worth, just like when having Fenris as totem while not being fenrir, you can still be in a pack with Fenris as totem. Plus no matter if your character becomes Star Gazer, he will always have lots of Fenrir inside him. You know learning gifts from a Totem's brood creates a special bonding with the torem that cannot be broken just by changing tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:27:21-07:00","id":1131075,"title":"","content":"I'm not 100% sure you won't lose gifts. Garous that become black spiral dancers don't keep their Gaian gifts even if they were part of the Garou, so it might make sense for a Storyteller to say that you lost them because the totem is angry. Also, some gifts may backfire spectacularly: yes, you've summoned 10 wolves through Horde of Valhalla, now look at them dismembering you since you made Fenris angry.<br /> <br /> That said, I think that you should not lose your gifts. But Fenris or his brood may get really angry when they realise (not if: when) you're still using their gifts and they might ask for some additional chimnage <i>for each tribe gift you have</i>. To keep their authorization to use high level gifts (rank 4+) the chimnage might take the shape of virtually endless servitude or nigh-suicidal missions, and not many werewolves may be interested in such a task.<br /> Telling the spirits &quot;nope&quot; it's not really an option, since even if you keep fighting all the angry spirits that come you'll someday meet an avatar of Great Fenris, and that's game over.<br /> <br /> Also: Fenris' brood may be willing to just break you because that's what they do, but different kind of spirits (like, Chimera's or Uktena's brood, maybe angry because you're using their gifts after learning them from another garou) could just decide to morph your life into a living hell. After all, Chimerlings are the ones teaching Malleable Spirit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 08-18-2017, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:59:44-07:00","id":1131094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1129130-changing-the-tribe?p=1131075#post1131075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not 100% sure you won't lose gifts. Garous that become black spiral dancers don't keep their Gaian gifts even if they were part of the Garou, so it might make sense for a Storyteller to say that you lost them because the totem is angry. Also, some gifts may backfire spectacularly: yes, you've summoned 10 wolves through Horde of Valhalla, now look at them dismembering you since you made Fenris angry.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gifts and rites of BSDs largely reflect inherent Wyrm taint, so the only way to undo being a BSD is to rip them away. Corruption tends to go far more easily on Gifts; when you go the other way, they change function, per W20 BotWyrm, if it would be appropriate to do so. Beyond the &quot;yank out the bad magic&quot;, though, it just doesn't happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:45:29-07:00","id":1131841,"title":"","content":"The only time I have ever seen mention of a Gift being 'lost' has been Trick Shot, and that was only for misuse of the Gift. (Which means you get one shot at being the best Sniper on the planet, but it'll be the last time you use that Gift.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T16:37:09-07:00","id":1131945,"title":"","content":"Another time losing gifts have been mentioned was in &quot;Cleansing Flame of Helios&quot; from Rage Across the Heavens, where any BSD hit by the gift has to make a stamina roll (or die) then a gnosis roll (or lose all taint, and wyrm related gifts and rites).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}